Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"deedee|And my girls! Come here, come here.":"","grace|Deedee. They're on your head.":"","deedee|Where are my reading glasses? I had them one second ago. I need to read the timer.":"","deedee|So they are. Not one word to Boppy.":"","deedee|A sliver for me. Just a sliver. Sourdough gives me gas.":"","tom|Mom, EVERYTHING gives you gas.":"","tom|The jar gets fifty grams of flour. You get the whole week.":"","tom|...And you steamed my shirts for the flight. You win. You always win.":"","tom|Things have to move.":"","tom|Everybody says goodbye. Then they come back. That's what planes are for.":"","deedee|Not one pepper for me either. Peppers give me gas.":"","grace|Deedee. EVERYTHING gives you gas.":"","deedee|Who told you that.":"","grace|Tata. At the crisp.":"","deedee|Tata is on thin ice.":"","rose|Apron pocket, Deedee!":"","deedee|Hand me my glasses. I want to look at him properly. Where ARE my glasses.":"","deedee|Thank you, Rosie. Now. Let me look at him.":"","tnb|And there's a scrap of paper in here. A drawing of one acorn. And one word: TAP TAP.":"","tnb|And there's a scrap of paper in here. A drawing of three acorns. And one word: CHITTER.":"","tom|It's beautiful. You can cry a little. I'll wait.":"","tom|...It's also freezing in here, and it's seventy-four degrees outside.":"","tom|A pilot light. A tiny blue flame, floating right there. That is Mr. Washington’s stove. That's the gumbo.":"","tom|A pilot light. A tiny blue flame, floating right there. That is Olivia’s stove. That's the lasagna.":"","boppy|You're wearing them, Dee.":"","deedee|Somebody read me that plaque. My glasses are in my other purse.":"","deedee|Oh. So I am. Well then.":"","deedee|I couldn't FIND them, honey.":"","boppy|Eleven times. Without her glasses. Eleven.":"","deedee|None for me, Justin. Store-bought gives me gas.":"","rose|Deedee! EVERYTHING gives you GAS!":"","deedee|Fine. One slice. For the girl who said it.":"","deedee|And has anybody seen my glasses? I can't read the oven.":"","rose|They're on the BUTTER, Deedee.":"","deedee|Of course they are. Nobody touch the butter.":"","deedee|Have you seen my reading glasses? I had them a minute ago. I've looked everywhere. Twice.":"","deedee|Found my glasses. They were in the fridge. Don't ask. Who wants a cookie?":"","skeeter|Brr! Tiny! Angry!":"","boppy|She's looking for her glasses again. They're on her head. I'm not saying anything. I'm saying it to you.":"","skeeter|We came in the freezer. It was cold. We're STILL cold.":"","skeeter|...I'm resting on a scoop. Don't tell him.":"","mudling|Glorp. These scoops are mine. He said so.":"","mudling|Blue raspberry isn't a fruit. I know. I don't care.":"","mudling|...Melting. Give me a minute. Glorp.":"","toad|Mint chip. Say it. MINT. CHIP.":"","toad|We hold the scoops. We hold the cow. We hold EVERYTHING.":"","toad|...Crunch. Regrouping. Crunch.":"","brainfreeze|Nothing melts in here. Nothing changes. Nothing LEAVES.":"","brainfreeze|...Hum. Hum. Hum. I am a freezer. I hum.":"","sal|The creamery is at the top of the Square. Go get those scoops.":"","sal|Airport? On the birthday? Your sister would find me. On foot. In the dark.":"","amy|Also. I've been standing still for four minutes and it's killing me. Want a running partner out there?":"","amy|Finally. Try to keep up. I mean that with love.":"","amy|Fine. I'll do burpees until you change your mind.":"","amy|Somebody has to tag out. I can wait, but I'll be stretching the whole time.":"","deedee|All right, all right. The pies need me anyway. Come back for a cookie.":"","deedee|Oh, honey. Somebody has to stay and mind the house. Who's it going to be?":"","boppy|Good. Somebody grab my cap. And slow down. I was a champion, you know.":"","boppy|My stomach isn't right and the fish aren't biting. Want an old man along? Just don't walk too fast.":"","boppy|Suit yourself. The recliner and I have an understanding.":"","boppy|Somebody has to sit this one out. My stomach volunteers, but the rest of me is coming.":"","tnb|Heading out? I can come. I have my longboard, a bus pass and a garment bag. I'm ready for anything. Mostly costume emergencies.":"","tnb|Great. Let me grab my jacket. Oh. You have it. Let me grab my other jacket.":"","tnb|Okay. I'll be here, throwing bowls. Come back if anything cracks.":"","tnb|Somebody has to hold down the house. I vote the couch, but it has to be a person.":"","sal|Los Angeles again? Cab seven loves this run. She hums the whole way.":"","sal|The girls stay home. Amy's rule. I don't argue with Amy.":"","grace|Tata, you HAVE to be back for my meet. I already told everybody you're coming.":"","rose|My tooth is loose. Look. LOOK. Tata, you're not looking.":"","tom|I'll be at the meet. Front row. I'll make a sign.":"","boppy|Los Angeles again? My back just got home from the marsh.":"","tom|Rose, that's a very good tooth. Guard it with your life.":"","boppy|Go. If you see a pepper out there, bring it back. I'll judge it.":"","tom|...Boppy would hate it up here.":"","tom|Lie flat, warm nuts, and absolutely no fish.":"","sal|Airport. Your young man fixed my visor. He made me promise to drive careful. So I'm going the speed limit. Everybody hates it.":"","tnb|That's a wrap, babe. I have a five a.m. call and forty capes to steam.":"","tnb|Go survive conference night. Bring snacks. I packed you snacks. Check your bag.":"","tom|I'm not scared. I'm PREPARED. Those are different.":"","tom|Six hours. Then conference night. My sister has a clipboard.":"","sal|Back to Los Angeles. Your sister gave me a gold star for using my blinker.":"","sal|The girls stay home. School night. It's always a school night.":"","grace|Tata, Mom says I'm in charge while you're gone. Of Rose.":"","rose|She's NOT in charge of me. Tata, tell her. TELL her.":"","tom|That's how it's always worked. Trust me. I was there.":"","tom|Nobody is in charge of anybody. Your mom is in charge of everybody.":"","amy|I survived conference night. I can survive you leaving.":"","amy|Text me when you land. I'm timing the flight. Don't lose.":"","tom|Delta One. Nobody is grading me up here.":"","tom|The flight attendant asked what I wanted. I said a nap. She laughed. I was SERIOUS.":"","sal|LAX. I'm taking the long way. There are squirrels on the short way.":"","tnb|Bready Mercury is safe, the squirrels signed a treaty, and I owe the landlord a fence.":"","tom|Somewhere down there, a squirrel is plotting.":"","tom|Not my problem. For six whole hours.":"","tnb|Go. I'll feed the starter. Twice a day, room temperature, no squirrels. I wrote it down.":"","sal|Los Angeles again? I'm starting to think you live there.":"","sal|The girls stay home. School tomorrow. Library books are due.":"","grace|Tata, I checked out a book about Los Angeles. Now I'll know where you are. Every minute.":"","tom|Both excellent choices. Return them on time.":"","rose|I checked out a book about a pig. It's not about Los Angeles. It's better.":"","tom|That library has had enough excitement for one year.":"","tom|Six hours of quiet. The library would be proud.":"","tom|...I already miss Rose shushing everybody at full volume.":"","tnb|Forty loaves, zero leftovers. Not bad for two guys and one oven.":"","sal|Airport. No eating in my cab. I can smell the potluck on you. It smells amazing. Still no.":"","tnb|Go open your fancy letter. Wear the blue shirt. I fixed the button. You're welcome.":"","tom|A letter with a seal. Nobody sends a seal for good news.":"","tom|Or do they? Six hours to think about it. Great.":"","tom|Downtown LA. Seventy-two and sunny. I didn't have to check.":"","tom|Six hours, no fish, and a pepper to find for Boppy. In that order.":"","tom|Long Island. Quiet. Thursday is conference night. It won't stay quiet.":"","grace|Tata! You're BACK! That's TWO times!":"","grace|Mom made you a binder. It has TABS.":"","rose|Did you bring the snacks? Tata. The SNACKS.":"","rose|I'm checking NOW.":"","tom|TNB packed them. Check my bag. Carefully. He also packed a note.":"","tom|Downtown LA. Five hours and fifty-one minutes. Amy will want the number.":"","tom|...Is that a squirrel on the cab? That's a squirrel on the cab.":"","tom|Long Island. Quiet. Library quiet. That's a different kind.":"","rose|It said my name. It said ROSE. Then it said shhh.":"","grace|Tata! THREE times! The library's still whispering. I SAID so. In a text.":"","tom|Then we go find out what it wants. After a sandwich.":"","grace|I'm bringing a flashlight. And a pencil. For notes.":"","tom|Downtown LA. It smells like somebody's grill. Everybody's grill.":"","tom|TNB says bring an empty stomach and forty bread pans. I've got the stomach.":"","tom|Long Island. No moon tonight. Somebody's going to make that my problem.":"","grace|Tata! FOUR! I have a chart now. You're on it.":"","tom|A wax seal with a clock on it. I'd look at it a lot too.":"","rose|Deedee has your letter. She hasn't opened it. She's LOOKED at it. A lot.":"","rose|I named the seal Flippers.":"","bun|Here. For the road. Don't tell the grips.":"","fern|Except that one. That's Assistant Steve.":"","bun|Plain roast chicken. No salt, no skin, no sauce. I keep it for the grips. They're also picky.":"","kenji|It's not. But you're trying very hard, and I respect that.":"","bun|Craft services! Take a bagel. Take two. Nobody is counting. I'm counting.":"","fern|We opened in March. The pupuseria next door has been here since 1994. We're learning a lot.":"","fern|Today's special is celery. Doña Carmen says that's not a meal. She's right.":"","dolores|I have run the projector here for forty years. I've seen every movie twice.":"","dolores|Tonight it's a horror double feature. Your boyfriend would love it. You'd watch it through your fingers.":"","kit|We painted it black. The neighbors call it the haunted house. We're choosing to take that as a compliment.":"","grace|TATA! You're BACK!":"","rose|I'm the tallest! Giddyup, Tata!":"","tom|Oof, I'm finally here! At least the 6 hours went by fast on Delta One! ;)":"","rose|Come on, Tata! Let's go!":"","grace|It's limited edition. There are only two in the whole world. You can squeeze it!":"","rose|I already licked the spoon. Don't tell.":"","mudling|Blub. The pie went that way. You can't have it. Blub.":"","deedee|Everybody okay? Itchy isn't hurt. Keep walking.":"","rose|I'm not laughing. I'm giggling. It's different.":"","grump|That's IT. Soggy Slap. For the giggler.":"","deedee|That's my GOOD tin, you overgrown handbag!":"","tom|Nobody touches Deedee’s crisp. Everybody ready?":"","boppy|Keep it, Tom. For luck. The fish clearly didn't want it.":"","bigone|Glub. Fine. Take your tin. I'm going back in the pond to think about things.":"","tom|...He said he'd be home.":"","tnb|My call time got pushed to Thursday. The lead actor lost a shoe. I already found it. So I'm all yours.":"","tnb|She's been sitting on your porch since eight. I tried to take her to the loft. She refused.":"","tnb|I'll take it.":"","tnb|It was a battle plan. You just didn't know it yet.":"","mudling|Cough. Nice street. We're going to sit on it for a while. Forever, actually.":"","odette|Stirring. Stirring. The gumbo never has to be done, baby. Isn’t that nice?":"","tnb|She's made that gumbo every day for fifty years. It's never once been \"never done.\"":"","tom|Then that's where we're going. Nara, stay close.":"","tnb|Babe. Look north. It's all coming down off the hills.":"","skeeter|Street cleaning. Tuesday. Eight to ten. You didn't read the sign. And the smog says we can stay forever.":"","tnb|Well, well, well... looks like we're in a bit of a shaky situation.":"","tnb|The ground is humming. That's never a good sign. I've seen this movie forty-seven times.":"","bigone|...I'll let things move. A little. Two inches a year. That's my best offer.":"","bigone|Rumble. Fine. The pipes are clear. I'm going back under the hill to think about my choices.":"","washington|Funny. For a while there I didn't want anything to change. Then I remembered the best parts all came from things changing.":"","deedee|Back already! Look at you. Did they feed you out there? Never mind. I'll feed you.":"","grace|I'm bringing a notebook. For science. And for proof.":"","boppy|Tom. Good. Sit down. No. Don't sit down. We're going fishing.":"","deedee|I have three pies in, so I'm staying put. Do NOT let him eat peppers on an empty stomach.":"","boppy|I never eat peppers on an empty stomach. I eat them on a full stomach. Then it's empty.":"","oolong|The kettle also says it'll rain on Tuesday. The kettle is wrong a lot. Enjoy the pier.":"","boppy|...Sure. Sure I can. I just choose not to. It's bad for the stomach.":"","grace|Last one there's a soggy sock!":"","grace|It's been a minute. I wrote it down.":"","boppy|Tom holds the tackle box. I cast. The fish comes. Nobody talks. That's the system.":"","boppy|Deedee isn't here.":"","boppy|Pickled in 1989. Nobody takes Boppy’s peppers. NOBODY.":"","grace|Boppy, you're breathing kind of hard.":"","grace|Sundials can't tell the wrong time. That's not how sundials work.":"","tom|We take it slow. Iron-Gill’s wake goes northwest, toward those big reeds.":"","boppy|That's what I said.":"","tom|Then we ask it nicely to move. Iron-Gill isn't keeping that jar.":"","boppy|You're sitting on the way to Sundial Hollow. Shove over.":"","log|Make me. Slowly. I'm very heavy when wet. I'm always wet.":"","rose|Tata, it's a LOG with a BOOT.":"","grace|A secret boardwalk. Of course there's a secret boardwalk.":"","rose|Boppy, he's sad! And spicy!":"","boppy|Go on, you old bucket. Catch and release. I'll come by. No hooks.":"","grace|Technically he caught your jar, and then we caught him. I'm writing it down anyway. For proof.":"","grace|I have proof. It's in my notebook. With the time. From a sundial.":"","boppy|...Almost isn't eating. Almost is fine.":"","tnb|Look who flew in for my big day. I'm on a forty-minute lunch. I spent thirty of it on the Metro.":"","tom|Then we get Nara. Then I watch you be very important. I'm not joking.":"","tnb|Also, Olivia dropped Nara at your place again. Family trip to the desert. She's been howling at your front door since nine.":"","tnb|She's coming to set. I already asked. Nobody said yes, but nobody said no fast enough.":"","moss|I wave at everybody. That's the job. Go on in.":"","tnb|Ray, it's me. Wardrobe. I left eighty minutes ago. You waved.":"","tnb|Gone? It's a rack. It has wheels. It doesn't have ambitions.":"","tnb|She's never eaten anything that fast. Not even my shoe.":"","tnb|That's a closed set! She's not on the call sheet!":"","tom|She doesn't know that. Let her have this.":"","tnb|Those are the neatest cue cards I've ever seen. Is that calligraphy?":"","tnb|Stage 7 is locked from the inside, though. And every set out here has a Sprite on it wrecking the shoot. The crew can't work like this.":"","tom|It's very fast. And very loud.":"","tnb|That's every clapper I've ever met.":"","tnb|New York is clear. It never looked better. It's plywood.":"","tnb|Somebody killed the work lights. And look, the catwalk is up. You only raise a catwalk when you're hiding something up there.":"","tnb|Babe. It's a megaphone in a beret. It has notes.":"","tom|This is a closed set. And you're not on the call sheet.":"","tnb|Forty. I counted. I'm going to count again. Forty.":"","tom|You're a professional. A crying professional. I'm so proud of you.":"","tnb|I'm going to cry. I'm not going to cry. I'm a professional. I'm crying a little.":"","la_woman|TNB, the studio wants you to have this. Gold-plated. It's the steamer from the lot’s very first wardrobe department.":"","tnb|You're the only uncle.":"","tom|Which makes me the good one. By default. I'll take it.":"","la_woman|And crew jackets. Wrap Party Jackets. Only the crew gets one. You're crew now. Even the dog.":"","amy|Two coffees. Both mine. Here, have one. That's how much I need you tonight.":"","tom|You brought me coffee. At night. That's a cry for help.":"","amy|It's conference night. Thirty parents at seven o’clock. And the school has lost its mind.":"","amy|On little paper legs. Mrs. Kowalski saw it. She's still upset about it.":"","amy|Everybody is coming. I have a clipboard, and I'm not afraid to use it.":"","grace|Doors don't just not open. That's not how doors work.":"","amy|Principal Pruitt, my brother Tom. He's very good in a crisis. He's also very calm about it, which is annoying.":"","grace|The gym isn't a room. It's a gym. It has a number anyway.":"","amy|Girls. That's excellent detective work. Gold stars. Both of you.":"","justin|Take some for the road. Don't tell Gary.":"","justin|Every conference night. Twelve years. It's the only reason Gary shows up.":"","amy|I've never been late in my life. Not once. Not even when I was born. I was early.":"","grace|You can't glue a xylophone. That's not how xylophones work.":"","amy|The Gregori Rule. No throwing at teachers. It's still on the wall.":"","amy|You know I was terrified of that thing? Every Friday. That's why I threw so hard.":"","michael|Mrs. Gregori’s brother, please go into the Cafetorium. Thank you. ...ksssh.":"","amy|That's the conference sign-up sheet. Thirty parents are waiting for it.":"","tom|That's her teacher voice. I'd listen.":"","amy|I'm going to count to three, and you're going to put the sheet down. One.":"","amy|...It's going to my desk. Of course it's going to my desk.":"","grump|Click. Fine. FINE. Pencils down. I'm going back in my cup.":"","grace|The sign-up sheet! It's a bit crumpled. And look, Tata. Something is taped to the bottom.":"","rose|Can we keep it? I'll keep it inside Lamby.":"","amy|Principal Pruitt, I can't take this.":"","amy|...I'm taking it. Thank you.":"","michael|This is for you. My Golden Stopwatch. Thirty-one Field Days. It's never once stopped early.":"","rose|Tata. Tata. There's a man.":"","michael|And Field Day shirts. Staff shirts. You're all staff now. Even the small loud ones.":"","grace|I'm keeping a list too. Mine has a chart.":"","amy|Probably a parent. A late one. There's always a late one.":"","tom|I didn't picture acorns.":"","tnb|Okay. Hi. Missed you. Don't panic. Look at the island.":"","tom|...Where's Bready Mercury.":"","tnb|That's the thing. I came over to feed him, like you asked. The jar was gone. The window was open.":"","tnb|I know, babe. I've seen every horror movie ever made. This is exactly how they start.":"","tnb|Olivia texted me too. Nara hasn't slept in three days. She just stands at the window and growls at trees.":"","tom|Nara is scared of the vacuum. Nara doesn't growl at trees.":"","amy|Whoever it is has very neat tape. Look at those corners.":"","bigone|Fine. FINE. That’s a wrap. On me. I'm going back in the prop closet.":"","boppy|He's a FISH, kiddo.":"","boppy|And I'm bringing THIS. My pepper jar. Homegrown, pickled in 1989. Older than your mother.":"","boppy|Excuse me? Nobody gets past ME. That's MY line. I was saying that at Rikers before you were a knot.":"","boppy|I'm breathing EXACTLY as hard as I want to.":"","boppy|That's no perch. That's OLD IRON-GILL. I saw him in 1994! I TOLD everybody!":"","boppy|Why is everybody walking like they're going to a fire? Slow down! My stomach is doing flips!":"","carmen|The pupusas are fine. Everything is fine. It's always this afternoon. Why did I ever flip them?":"","grace|Tata! Deedee made rhubarb crisp for you. It's cooling RIGHT NOW.":"","grace|Tata, you're staying the WHOLE week, right?":"","grump|...Don't try to be nice to me. Nobody is nice to me. I'll PINCH.":"","grump|Grrrumble. You're standing in my puddle. And the small one is LAUGHING at me.":"","grump|Snarl. Somebody cast me badly in 1997. I've been in a knot ever since. Nobody gets past ME.":"","la_woman|The rack! The costumes! We can shoot! We're shooting! That's a WRAP on today, everybody!":"","log|Creak. This was a boardwalk once. Now it's MY spot. Everything catches on me here. I like it.":"","log|DING! You're LATE! Everybody is late! I ring and I ring and nobody is ever on time!":"","michael|(on the intercom) ...ksssh... Attention, please. The Cafetorium doors are OPEN. Parents, please wait in the hall. There's something in the Cafetorium.":"","mudling|Squelch. Have you seen my other sock? It looks just like me. It's ALSO angry.":"","mudling|Squelch. I glued the piano. I glued the xylophone. I glued a recorder to a tuba. It's ART.":"","dot|TNB! TNB! The rack! Rack two! It's GONE.":"","dot|WRAP PARTY AT CRAFTY! Toni made a cake! It's shaped like a clapper! It's not clapping!":"","grace|FOR EVERYONE, LOVE DEEDEE. That's Deedee’s handwriting! Everyone means us!":"","grace|It MOVED. Shadows don't move like that. I'm writing this down. In pen.":"","grace|It's the AFTERNOON. The sun is right there. Sundials can't be wrong. That's not how sundials work.":"","grace|Okay, everybody. Tata is in front. I'm in charge of choreography. FIGHT!":"","rose|It's covered in RED.":"","rose|Mom. Mom. Are we going to SCHOOL? At NIGHT? That's the best thing that ever happened.":"","rose|Tata, it's SPARKLY. I love it. I hate it. I love it.":"","rose|Tata, it's a PEN. With GLASSES.":"","tnb|And there's a scrap of paper in here. A drawing of two acorns. And one word: SCRATCH.":"","tnb|That's a costume tag. That's MY tag. WARDROBE, RACK 2, HAND WASH ONLY. I underlined it twice.":"","tom|Nara. NARA. Don't...":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"deedee":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"9UrcxKDUU0pvcnFhdfTU","name":"AoT Deedee (picked 2026-10-28)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"grace":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"","designed":false,"voice_id":"JVVJ6VsnUPJAdfGmEBGP","name":"AoT Grace (Gretchen)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85}},"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"rose":{"voice_id":"ocZQ262SsZb9RIxcQBOj","name":"Lulu Lolipop - High-Pitched and Bubbly  (female, young, american, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"boppy":{"voice_id":"QzTKubutNn9TjrB7Xb2Q","name":"Jerry B. - New York Italian Mobster  (male, middle_aged, new york, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":1},"direction":"deep gravelly voice","designed":false},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"brainfreeze":{"voice_id":"kYM9iwUI7t87mhAOBs1T","name":"AoT Brain Freeze","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon villain who is a walking chest freezer: a flat, cold, humming monotone with a slight metallic buzz, deadpan and sulky, slow and heavy, with a lonely sadness underneath that cracks through when he is surprised. Animated character voice."},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."},"amy":{"model":"eleven_v4","direction":"heavy Long Island accent","designed":false,"voice_id":"HLSHrV3D7Gp6sEFcHNev","name":"AoT Amy (Kind)","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8}},"bun":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":""},"fern":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":""},"kenji":{"voice_id":"Pp9gl3BrnVq62dIWU2sx","name":"AoT Justin (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":""},"dolores":{"voice_id":"5nPpmcfu7pDFPztXuQIJ","name":"AoT Aunt Ellie (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":""},"kit":{"voice_id":"zROpM0X5rfQMe4CN4C7f","name":"AoT Bean","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":""},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"odette":{"voice_id":"ubIjwev8dFIC3TyJqJPC","name":"AoT Miss Odette","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her seventies with a rich, warm, musical voice and a light Louisiana Creole accent. Runs a soul food kitchen, calls everyone baby, unhurried and loving with a sly sense of humor. Clean studio recording."},"carmen":{"voice_id":"8ncJvaxiyfELP457mBLS","name":"AoT Doña Carmen","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her sixties with a warm, firm, proud voice and a light Salvadoran Spanish accent. Runs a pupuseria, generous and no-nonsense, laughs easily. Clean studio recording."},"washington":{"voice_id":"ARRjeRIXQjOrcraWRDoq","name":"AoT Mr. Washington","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly man in his eighties with a deep, warm, slow voice and a gentle hint of Louisiana in it. A neighborhood storyteller on his porch, unhurried, kind, a little gravelly. Clean studio recording."},"oolong":{"voice_id":"2PhKaj7sDKqdDEhqQyhl","name":"AoT Oolong","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly woman in her seventies with a warm, gossipy, conspiratorial voice and a light British accent. Leans in to share secrets, little cackle of a laugh, cozy and sly. Clean studio recording."},"log":{"voice_id":"DmA9AOv6Fsic2LQdqVVM","name":"AoT Log Lump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A sleepy cartoon log creature, very slow, deep, woody and drowsy voice, yawning between words, mumbly and content. Animated character voice."},"moss":{"voice_id":"7vp7iK3I8DiDLgC90c3t","name":"AoT Moss","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall, gentle man in his thirties with a deep, slow, mellow American voice. Dreamy and laid back, long pauses, quietly pleased with his own puns. Warm low tone. Clean studio recording."},"dot":{"voice_id":"gYzudf4C0nXnEecqXK5t","name":"AoT Dot","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small woman in her forties with a quick, crisp, precise American voice, slightly nasal. Talks fast in short exact phrases like she is reading a tally sheet. Proud of her accuracy. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"michael":{"voice_id":"24fSFWvKYGI0zVR7L6JQ","name":"AoT Michael","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall man in his early forties with a calm, low, dry American voice. A tech dad holding two kids, patient, deadpan, quietly funny, a little tired. Clean studio recording."},"justin":{"voice_id":"Pp9gl3BrnVq62dIWU2sx","name":"AoT Justin (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his early forties with an easygoing, friendly voice, Long Island born with a slight country twang. Goofy proud dad, handyman, sports fan, relaxed and warm, quick to laugh. Clean studio recording."},"olivia":{"voice_id":"3KdkB2LF6PUw0muuS0j7","name":"AoT Olivia","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her late thirties with a quick, bright, articulate American voice. A journalist and mom of two little kids, talks fast, wry and warm, always half distracted. Clean studio recording."},"penny":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a fast-talking, bright, enthusiastic American saleswoman voice. Quick patter, playful, warm and a little pushy, every line a pitch. Clean studio recording."},"page":{"voice_id":"UnNThlnnIcLaHiWDpFdl","name":"AoT Page","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his forties, a librarian with a hushed, dry, whispery American voice. Speaks very quietly and precisely, mildly scandalized by everything, droll. Soft breathy whisper. Clean studio recording."},"ellie":{"voice_id":"5nPpmcfu7pDFPztXuQIJ","name":"AoT Aunt Ellie (Long Island)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A very elderly woman in her nineties with a grand, theatrical, sharp-witted voice and an old-school Long Island New York accent. Dry, imperious and glamorous, slow deliberate delivery, every line a bon mot. Clean studio recording."},"luna":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a dreamy, slow, wonder-filled American voice. Soft and spacey, drifting pauses, sincere awe with a touch of embarrassment. Clean studio recording."},"pistachio":{"voice_id":"LyoSZrqTSG25l7i0uBGl","name":"AoT Mr. Pistachio","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late fifties with a warm, hearty Long Island New York accent, an ice cream shop owner who loves his regulars, booming friendly laugh, talks with his hands, a little dramatic about his scoops. Clean studio recording."},"pip":{"voice_id":"BI45NIQbK17XdpKBL2Kq","name":"AoT Pip","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A young woman in her twenties with a soft, earnest, slightly breathy American voice. Sweet and a little odd, very sincere, speaks gently and protectively like she is talking about a beloved pet. Clean studio recording."},"gus":{"voice_id":"CcabrpeMRBXae9HlsCuq","name":"AoT Gus","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An old man in his seventies with a slow, warm, slightly creaky American voice. Deadpan and dignified, treats sitting on a bench like serious athletic training. Unhurried. Clean studio recording."},"bean":{"voice_id":"zROpM0X5rfQMe4CN4C7f","name":"AoT Bean","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late twenties with an upbeat, rambling, friendly American voice. A little scattered, quick bursts of words, cheerful and unbothered. Light and bright. Clean studio recording."},"boomie2":{"voice_id":"rrjdoujYPDo3FGeRqm3Q","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A young Black American woman in her late thirties to early fourties with a warm, rich, low alto voice, smooth and a little husky, deeper than most women’s voices. A gospel and soul singer, kind and bubbly, laughs from the belly, slides into song mid-sentence. Clean studio recording."},"boomie":{"voice_id":"FgGtmhYdBou3a14mKYgx","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a big, warm, rich singer’s voice, bubbly and motherly, slides into song mid-sentence, laughs from the belly. Clean studio recording."}});
